In .NET 10, MAUI adopted Android's edge-to-edge display by default, which deprecates `adjustResize`. The fix is to react to keyboard (IME) insets and adjust your layout's bottom padding.

**Recommended approach — handle IME insets in your Android platform code:**

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Android.OS.Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new KeyboardInsetsListener());
    }

    private class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View view, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

            // Use whichever is larger — keyboard or nav bar
            int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);
            view.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottomPadding);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

**Layout tip** — structure your chat page so the input bar is at the bottom of a `Grid`:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

**Key points:**
- `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` tracks the software keyboard rect
- When the keyboard opens, `imeInsets.Bottom` grows, pushing your content up
- On iOS this isn't needed — MAUI already adjusts for the keyboard automatically
- You can remove any old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust` calls from `MauiProgram.cs`
